-- title:
--   Exactness of Fontaine's functor along a Hopf-kernel extension
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative ring $\mathcal O$ in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\mathcal R$, $\mathcal R_1$, $\mathcal R_3$ be commutative rings carrying cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra structures and finite free as $\mathcal O$-modules, with $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R$ and $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R_1$ powers of $p$, and assume the Cartier dual $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathbb Z/p}(\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R,\mathbb Z/p)$ is a local ring. Let $\pi:\mathcal R\to\mathcal R_1$ be a surjective bialgebra map and $j:\mathcal R_3\to\mathcal R$ an injective bialgebra map whose image, as an $\mathcal O$-subalgebra, is the Hopf kernel of $\pi$, i.e. the equaliser of $(\mathrm{id}\otimes\pi)\circ\Delta_{\mathcal R}$ and $r\mapsto r\otimes 1$. Write $M(\cdot)$ for the Dieudonné module over $\mathbb Z/p$ at $p$, the direct limit over $n$ of the additive subgroups of truncated Witt vectors of length $n$ on the given algebra cut out by the condition that the map induced by comultiplication equals the sum of the maps induced by the two inclusions, and $L(\cdot)\subseteq M(\cdot)$ for the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of classes representable at some level $n$ by an element lying in `fontaineKer` for the base-change map $r\mapsto 1\otimes r$. Then: $M(\mathrm{id}_{\mathbb Z/p}\otimes\pi)$ is surjective; $M(\mathrm{id}_{\mathbb Z/p}\otimes j)$ is injective; the composite $M(\mathrm{id}\otimes\pi)\circ M(\mathrm{id}\otimes j)$ vanishes identically; every $z\in L(\mathcal R_1)$ is $M(\mathrm{id}\otimes\pi)(y)$ for some $y\in L(\mathcal R)$; and any $x\in M(\mathbb Z/p\otimes_{\mathcal O}\mathcal R_3)$ with $M(\mathrm{id}\otimes j)(x)\in L(\mathcal R)$ lies in $L(\mathcal R_3)$.
--
--   This is the exactness of Fontaine's functor $G\mapsto (L(G),M(G_{\mathbb F_p}))$ on an extension of unipotent finite flat commutative $p$-group schemes presented by a closed immersion together with its Hopf kernel, the surjectivity in the first clause being right exactness of the Dieudonné module functor over the perfect field $\mathbb F_p$. It feeds the construction of Fontaine–Conrad presentations for locally flat cocycles and, through that, the bound on the rank of Hecke torsion used in the local study of the deformation problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_map_baseChange_surjective_injective_fontaineHodge_of_range_eq_hopfKer.lean

